From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: evict stale duplicate-key ehash record before insert (A6-LOSS)

fman_pcd_ehash_add_key() always LIFO head-inserted a new hardware flow
record, with no check for a live record already keyed on the same
5-tuple. ask.ko's PR14r REPLACE dedup is keyed on the nf_conn cookie,
not the 5-tuple -- a conntrack churn event (e.g. SYN-retransmit races
under bidirectional load) can hand the same 5-tuple a new cookie, which
sails past that dedup and calls fman_pcd_fe_flow_add() again. The
second call produced a second live hardware record for the same key:
the new one became the reachable bucket head, the old one became an
orphaned chain tail -- still DMA-resident, never hit again by
hardware, and never freed (fman_pcd_ehash_del_key() stops at the first
key match in list order, so only one of the duplicates is ever
reclaimed on teardown).

Confirmed live via fe_ehash_stats polling on .185 during a 60s
bidirectional iperf3 run, 2026-10-06: several ehash records sat frozen
at single-digit pkt_count while sibling records in the same table
climbed by hundreds of thousands of packets over the same window.
Records from an already-finished prior test were also still present
and frozen in a later dump, confirming the leak persists across
teardown, not just across inserts. This is the suspected mechanism
behind the retransmit storm described in plans/ASK2-VS-VENDOR-THROUGHPUT.md
(A6-LOSS): under heavy bidirectional load the second SYN of a
retransmit race wins a new cookie, orphans the original record's slot,
and any traffic still hashing to the orphan during the churn window is
dropped until the flow's next REPLACE.

Fix: before the unconditional insert, call fman_pcd_ehash_del_key() for
the same key to evict any existing record first, so at most one live
record ever exists per key. fman_pcd_ehash_del_key() requires the
caller to already hold pcd->fe_lock -- true for every current caller of
fman_pcd_ehash_add_key() (fman_pcd_fe_flow_add() and the debugfs
"add"/"add drop"/"add stats" commands all take the lock before calling
in), so no new locking is introduced here.

Signed-off-by: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index ef56c7f9f98d..e68ecf4fa4ed 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -2283,6 +2283,13 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key_natwrap_dbgfs(
 	return fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(t, key, key_size, enq_off, fqid, stats,
 				      l2_dst, l2_src, eth_type, NULL, vlan);
 }
+/* F-219 (A6-LOSS, 2026-10-06): forward decl so fman_pcd_ehash_add_key()
+ * below can evict a stale same-key record before inserting a new one.
+ * See the F-219 comment at its call site for the defect this closes.
+ */
+static int fman_pcd_ehash_del_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
+				  const u8 *key, u8 key_size);
+
 static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				  const u8 *key, u8 key_size,
 				  u32 enq_off, u32 fqid, bool stats,
@@ -2303,6 +2310,30 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 	if (key_size > FMAN_EHASH_FLOW_KEY_MAX)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/*
+	 * F-219 (A6-LOSS): this function used to unconditionally LIFO
+	 * head-insert, even when a live record for this exact key already
+	 * existed (ask.ko's REPLACE-dedup is keyed on the nf_conn cookie,
+	 * not the 5-tuple key -- a conntrack churn event that hands the
+	 * same 5-tuple a new cookie bypasses it, e.g. SYN-retransmit races
+	 * under bidirectional load). The stale record then became an
+	 * orphaned bucket-chain tail: never hit again by hardware, never
+	 * freed by fman_pcd_ehash_del_key() (which stops at the first
+	 * key match in list order and only ever reaps one of the
+	 * duplicates). Confirmed live via fe_ehash_stats on .185,
+	 * 2026-10-06: several records frozen at single-digit pkt_count
+	 * while sibling records in the same table climbed by hundreds of
+	 * thousands over the same window. Evict any existing record for
+	 * this key first, so at most one live record per key ever exists.
+	 */
+	{
+		int drc = fman_pcd_ehash_del_key(t, key, key_size);
+
+		if (!drc)
+			pr_info_ratelimited("fman_pcd: F-219 ehash evicted stale duplicate record for key before re-insert (key_size=%u)\n",
+					    key_size);
+	}
+
 	index = fman_pcd_ehash_bucket_index(key, key_size, t->hash_shift,
 					    t->hash_mask);
 
